Z||000000||87ECO5||12-10-2001||04:08 PM||||It's 20 minutes long which translates into outrageous download times for those with dialup.<P>Nevertheless, really worth seeing:<P> <A HREF="http://www.calpilot.com/worldtrade.swf" TARGET=_blank>http://www.calpilot.com/worldtrade.swf</A> <P>Sorry if this is a dupe.<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 12-10-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000001||Ken Wittlief||12-10-2001||04:46 PM||||Something I have been thinking about for a while. I noticed a long time ago that very often people get caught in a robbery situation or hostage situation, or a Colinbine kind of thing, and end up being executed /shot one by one, or killed while trying to flee.<P> I decided before 9/11 that if I am ever in such a situation that I am not going down without a fight, AND if there are other lives in danger, I am NOT going to flee either! There is an old gun safety rule - 'never point a gun at someone unless you intend to kill them' <P> I think a corrally of that is, 'if someone points a gun at you they intend to kill you'.<P> So if I find myself in that perdictament, I will assume I am already dead anyway, so I might as well do as much damage to the perperator as possible - maybe I can take him with me, or maybe I can only buy several seconds - keeping him busy killing me will give others the chance to flee, and maybe to live instead of die.<P> Maybe we need an organization of people who feel the same way - maybe we should name it after one of the guys on flight 93, or after the flight itself -the 93'ers?!<P> Towards this end I carry a folding pocket knife that has a 4" blade and looks like a hunting knife when opened. We cant all carry conceled guns with us everywhere. We can take some martial arts training.<P> But I think the most important thing is to have it already decided in your mind before it happens, in case it ever happens - to act quickly and decively, knowing it will probabally cost you your own life<P> but in doing so you might save the lives of other victums.<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 12-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||12-11-2001||09:55 AM||||ok now this is Creep Pea.<P>I run webshots desktops (free software that puts up new wallpaper everyday and has a screen saver that runs a jpeg slideshow - <A HREF="http://www.webshots.com)" TARGET=_blank>www.webshots.com)</A> <P> and I have about 200 jpegs in the photo list<P> today for wallpaper it puts up a jpeg of a catamaran sailing in NY harbor with the WTC in the background, the only shot with the WTC out of my 200 jpegs.<P> today, 12/11 - 3 months.||||reg||1
